# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in real values. Run `docker compose up -d` first
# for the local Postgres/Redis ports below. See docs/conventions.md for details.

# Primary Postgres connection. Points at PgBouncer (docker-compose "pgbouncer" service, port
# 6432) and NOT at Postgres directly (5432), because that is how the deployed app connects and a
# pooler that is only in the path in production is a pooler nobody has tested. Transaction
# pooling mode: nothing may rely on session state, which is why the draft lock is a row lock and
# not pg_advisory_lock. See docs/decisions/data-layer-hardening.md.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://commish:commish@localhost:6432/commish

# Redis, used for the Streams → SSE real-time mechanism (docker-compose "redis" service, port 6379).
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# WorkOS AuthKit: hosted sign-in/up, sessions, MFA, OAuth. From the WorkOS dashboard.
WORKOS_CLIENT_ID=client_replace_me

# WorkOS API key. From the WorkOS dashboard.
WORKOS_API_KEY=sk_replace_me

# Session cookie encryption password. Must be at least 32 characters.
WORKOS_COOKIE_PASSWORD=replace_me_with_a_random_string_of_32_or_more_characters

# WorkOS redirect URI after hosted sign-in; must match the WorkOS dashboard configuration.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKOS_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/callback

# Optional. Fallback origin for absolute links this server mints for someone who is NOT already
# in the app (a commissioner's invite URL, `POST /api/leagues/[leagueId]/invites`). Normally
# unused: the route reads the origin straight off the incoming request (`originFor`, that file),
# which already carries the real Host header in dev and behind a proxy alike. This only matters
# if a request ever arrives with no parseable URL at all — commented out rather than shipped
# empty, because an uncommented empty line looks configured.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Salts the hash of the request address stored on each sign-in's session signal. The app never
# stores an address in the clear, only sha256(salt + address), so this value has to be a real
# secret and not a constant. Generate one with openssl rand -hex 32 and never commit the real
# value. Required at every sign-in; there is no fallback.
SESSION_SIGNAL_SALT=replace_me_with_a_random_string

# Which stats source `npm run seed` reads: mock (default) or tank01. Mock is the fixed 2026
# dataset committed at src/stats/mock/dataset.json and needs no key or network. tank01 reads the
# live Tank01 NFL API and needs TANK01_API_KEY below. An unrecognized value fails fast and names
# the valid ones; it never falls back to mock, because a deployment that thinks it has live data
# and is quietly serving a fake season would look healthy and be wrong.
STATS_PROVIDER=mock

# Required only when STATS_PROVIDER=tank01. A RapidAPI key subscribed to the Tank01 NFL API
# (tank01-nfl-live-in-game-real-time-statistics-nfl). A paid tier is approved and the real key
# belongs in .env.local, not here; STATS_DAILY_REQUEST_BUDGET below stays at its default
# until the purchased daily quota is named, so raise it only once that number is known. Selecting
# tank01 without this fails fast and names this variable. Commented out rather than shipped
# empty, because an uncommented empty line looks configured.
# TANK01_API_KEY=

# Optional, only for STATS_PROVIDER=tank01. Which NFL season to read; defaults to the value in
# src/stats/tank01/config.ts. Tank01 holds 2022 onward, and 2026 means the 2026-27 season.
# TANK01_SEASON=2026

# Optional, only for STATS_PROVIDER=mock. Treats one week of the fixed 2026 dataset as still
# being played, so the live scoring surfaces can be seen without an API key. Every other week
# stays final. Leave it unset for the behavior Plan A shipped.
# MOCK_STATS_LIVE_WEEK=

# Optional. Overrides src/stats-pipeline/config.ts's ingestion mode (default final-only).
# live is the launch target: it fetches every non-final game every tick instead of each box score
# once, which costs several times what final-only does. Raise STATS_DAILY_REQUEST_BUDGET with
# it. See the arithmetic in STATS_INGESTION_CONFIG's docblock before turning this on.
# STATS_INGESTION_MODE=

# Optional. Overrides src/stats-pipeline/config.ts's poll interval in milliseconds (default
# 1,800,000, thirty minutes). Every tick costs at least one upstream request, so halving this
# doubles the day's schedule spending; check STATS_DAILY_REQUEST_BUDGET headroom first.
# STATS_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=

# Optional. Overrides src/stats-pipeline/config.ts's DAILY upstream request ceiling across
# ingestion and the season backfill together (default 500: the worst ingestion day plus one full
# season backfill, with headroom). RapidAPI meters the Tank01 plans per day. Set it to the
# PURCHASED daily quota: this is a ceiling on our own spending, not a claim about what the
# account allows, and setting it above the real quota only moves where the ledger stops
# protecting the key.
# STATS_DAILY_REQUEST_BUDGET=

# Which GIF source chat's "Add a GIF" button searches: none (default) or giphy. none means no
# provider at all: the composer never renders the button, and GET /api/gifs/search 404s, so
# chat is exactly what it always was, text and emoji, with no dead button and no broken search
# box. giphy needs GIPHY_API_KEY below. An unrecognized value fails fast and names the valid
# ones; it never falls back to none, the same reasoning STATS_PROVIDER documents above.
GIF_PROVIDER=none

# Required only when GIF_PROVIDER=giphy. A Giphy API key (developers.giphy.com). Commented out
# rather than shipped empty, because an uncommented empty line looks configured.
# GIPHY_API_KEY=

# Which payments rail the money seam (src/payments-provider/) talks to: mock is the default and
# the ONLY implementation this phase. The mock moves no money and hits no network. Real rails
# (Column / Aeropay / Paysafe) are founder-gated future implementations that must pass the seam's
# contract suite before their names may even appear here. An unrecognized value fails fast and
# names the valid ones; it never falls back to mock, because a deployment that thinks it is on a
# real money rail and is quietly accepting deposits into a mock would look healthy and be wrong
# in the worst way available.
PAYMENTS_PROVIDER=mock

# Required only when a real payments provider ships: the shared secret its webhook callbacks are
# HMAC-SHA256-signed with (verified by src/payments-provider/ingest.ts). While
# PAYMENTS_PROVIDER=mock this may stay unset — the mock signs and verifies with a committed
# dev-only constant that protects nothing because the mock moves nothing. Commented out rather
# than shipped empty, because an uncommented empty line looks configured.
# PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Which KYC bureau the identity-verification seam (src/payments-provider/kyc-*.ts) talks to: mock
# is the default and the ONLY implementation this phase. The mock verifies no real identity and
# hits no network. A real bureau (Persona / Alloy class) is a founder-gated future implementation
# that must pass src/payments-provider/kyc-contract-suite.ts unchanged before its name may even
# appear here — the same fail-fast, never-silently-mock rule PAYMENTS_PROVIDER follows above.
KYC_PROVIDER=mock

# Dev-only opt-in for the destructive seeders (`npm run seed`, scripts/drive-dev-draft.ts).
# They mass-upsert players and create dev_user_* placeholder rows, so they refuse to run
# unless this is exactly "1" AND DATABASE_URL above names a loopback host.
ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE_SEED=1

# Dev-only: set to your real (WorkOS) user id after signing in once and `npm run seed` hands
# you team 1 and the commissioner's chair in the seeded leagues. Commented out rather than
# shipped as an empty line: `src/data/seed/index.ts` reads it with `envOrUndefined`, which
# treats an empty value as absent, but an uncommented empty line still LOOKS configured.
# DEV_SEED_CLAIM_USER_ID=

# Test-only: Postgres connection used by the test suite (docker-compose "postgres-test" service,
# port 5433, tmpfs). Direct, not pooled, on purpose: a pooler in the path makes every test slower
# and can turn a real regression into something that looks like a pooling artifact. The suite is
# run through TEST_PGBOUNCER_URL explicitly as its own verification step instead.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://commish:commish@localhost:5433/commish_test

# Test-only: the same test database reached through PgBouncer in transaction pooling mode
# (docker-compose "pgbouncer-test" service, port 6433). src/db/pgbouncer.test.ts uses this.
# The pooler routes by connect-time database name (wildcard config — see docker-compose.yml),
# so a worktree lane on its own test database points this at that database's name instead.
TEST_PGBOUNCER_URL=postgres://commish:commish@localhost:6433/commish_test

# Optional: enables AI/LLM features (src/lib/llm/). Without it the AI draft moderator falls back
# to its static nudge and the lineup advisor answers from the app's own math (labelled "Offline
# advice"). Both surfaces are fully functional with no key; no feature is hidden, only its
# wording changes.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Dev-only: used by the browser-driven lab scripts (scripts/mint-dev-session.ts,
# scripts/lab-shot.ts), not required for normal development. mint-dev-session.ts writes an
# authenticated session to LAB_SESSION_FILE (default ./.lab-session.json, gitignored) using
# LAB_EMAIL/LAB_PASSWORD if set, or generates a throwaway email/CSPRNG password otherwise.
# lab-shot.ts then reads LAB_SESSION_FILE to take an authenticated screenshot. All three are
# commented out rather than shipped as empty lines: the scripts read them with `envOrUndefined`
# (`scripts/lib/env.ts`), which treats an empty value the same as an absent one, and LAB_EMAIL/
# LAB_PASSWORD must be set together or not at all (`mintLabSession` refuses one without the
# other).
# LAB_SESSION_FILE=./.lab-session.json
# LAB_EMAIL=
# LAB_PASSWORD=
# SHOWCASE_DRAFT_ID retired (Phase 3.6, Task 5): the front door's old live-draft-board preview
# was replaced by the real open-league shelf (`listPublicLeagues`) and the real proof strip
# (`proofStats`) — both queries, never a showcase render. `dev_draft_snake` still seeds (see
# `src/data/seed/config.ts`) for whatever else in the dev database expects a platform-owned
# draft to exist; nothing reads this env var anymore.

# The browser end-to-end suite (playwright.config.ts, e2e/) authenticates by minting a real
# WorkOS TEST-directory session from the three WORKOS_* values above, and refuses to run
# against anything but an "sk_test_" API key. In CI those come from the WORKOS_TEST_API_KEY /
# WORKOS_TEST_CLIENT_ID / WORKOS_TEST_COOKIE_PASSWORD repository secrets, and the e2e job stops
# with a visible warning when they are absent. There is no dev auth bypass to fall back on.

# Test-only: base URL the Playwright e2e suite (`npm run e2e`) drives, and the URL its
# `webServer` starts `next start` on (see playwright.config.ts). Defaults to
# http://localhost:3100, NOT 3000. Leave this line commented out unless port 3100 is also
# unavailable to you. `playwright.config.ts` reads it with `envOr`, which treats an empty value
# the same as an absent one, but the line is commented out anyway so a fresh clone never ships
# an env var that LOOKS configured but does nothing.
# E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3100

# Test-only, and NOT settable here: `playwright.config.ts` sets E2E_SHOW_FIXTURE_LEAGUES=1 on the
# `next start` process it spawns for the suite, and nothing else in this repo sets it. It tells
# `notAFixtureLeague()` (`@/league-service/browse`) to stop hiding leagues named `E2E …` or
# `Mobile360…`, because those specs join their own seeded league through the real `/browse` shelf.
# Documented here so the var is discoverable, deliberately left with no line to uncomment: setting
# it for the founder's dev server would put every leftover fixture back on the shelf, which is the
# exact junk the predicate exists to hide. Only the literal "1" opts in; the filter is otherwise on.

# NEXT_DIST_DIR is NOT read from this file: `npm run build` is a plain `next build`, not
# `dotenv -e .env.local -- next build`, so nothing here reaches it. It is a one-off shell
# prefix instead, set before a manual `npm run e2e`: `NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next-e2e npm run build`.
# That gives the build and the served app the SAME isolated dist dir playwright.config.ts
# already builds in (its webServer passes the same var to `next start`), instead of racing a
# concurrent `next dev`'s default ".next" (see next.config.ts). Every other command leaves it
# unset.
